course: dictionary
lesson: 12875
title: Ensemble: a group that works as one
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ensemble is a group of people or things that work together as one whole. The word comes from French, where it means «together».
explain: Read the clues around the word: «The school ensemble played three songs at the concert.» School, played, songs and concert tell you the ensemble is a group of musicians, so it means a small group that performs together.
explain: The same word can mean a set of clothes worn together: «Her ensemble was a red dress with a matching scarf.» Matching and dress show it is an outfit. Always check the clues to see which meaning fits.
explain: To test your meaning, swap in a simple word such as group or outfit. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: An ensemble is a small group of musicians, singers, dancers or actors who perform together.
fact: An ensemble can also be a set of clothes that are worn together as one outfit.
fact: «The ensemble cast» means the actors in a play or film who work together as a team.
fact: Ensemble can mean a group of things seen as a whole, like a picture made from many small parts.
fact: The word ensemble comes from French and means «together».
exercise: «The school ensemble played three songs at the concert.» What is an ensemble here? | A kind of school bell | *A small group of musicians who play together | A single loud drum | A ticket to the concert
exercise: «Her ensemble was a red dress with a matching scarf.» What does ensemble mean here? | A group of dancers | *An outfit of clothes worn together | A piece of music | A party for her friends
exercise: The word ensemble comes from French. What does it mean? | Dance | Music | *Together | Alone
test: «The ensemble cast of the play took a bow together.» Which word tells you that ensemble means a group of actors? | bow | end | together | *cast
test: Which sentence uses ensemble to mean a group of things seen as a whole? | «The ensemble ate its lunch at noon.» | «The ensemble was very cold and wet.» | *«The ensemble of tiny shells made a lovely picture on the shelf.» | «The ensemble ran fast around the field.»
exam: In «The wind ensemble practised every Tuesday», which word could replace ensemble and keep the meaning? | pillow | puddle | sandwich | *band
